h alone; his daily cleanups grew into a 100-volunteer movement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133034407.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Houston resident's initiative to clean up neglected areas has blossomed into a vibrant volunteer movement. With one hundred dedicated individuals now on board, their mission is to remove illegally dumped waste. Collaborating with local organizations and harnessing the power of social media, city officials and law enforcement are boosting efforts to tackle this pressing issue, ultimately enhancing the community's aesthetics and the well-being of its residents.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-houston-man-began-clearing-illegally-dumped-trash-alone-his-daily-cleanups-grew-into-a-100-volunteer-movement/articleshow/133034407.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/one-houston-man-began-clearing-illegally-dumped-trash-alone-his-daily-cleanups-grew-into-a-100-volunteer-movement/articleshow/133034407.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T18:51:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133035155,imgsize-1595001.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Video: 2 injured after gunman opens fire near New York subway station]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133034524.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/video-2-injured-after-gunman-opens-fire-near-new-york-subway-station/articleshow/133034524.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/video-2-injured-after-gunman-opens-fire-near-new-york-subway-station/articleshow/133034524.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T18:38:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133034980,imgsize-1384978.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists watched a 1km-wide, 100m-thick section of Greenland’s Sorgenfri glacier break away]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133033581.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a striking display of nature, a massive section of a Greenland glacier detached and collapsed into the sea, captured by scientists on a research vessel. This occurrence unfolded as part of a study examining the implications of meltwater runoff on major ocean currents. Advanced autonomous robots are being utilized to collect vital data from the hazardous ice face.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-aboard-rrs-sir-david-attenborough-watched-a-1km-wide-100m-thick-section-of-greenlands-sorgenfri-glacier-break-away-weighing-an-estimated-18-million-tonnes/articleshow/133033581.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-aboard-rrs-sir-david-attenborough-watched-a-1km-wide-100m-thick-section-of-greenlands-sorgenfri-glacier-break-away-weighing-an-estimated-18-million-tonnes/articleshow/133033581.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T18:13:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133034362,imgsize-667420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[H-1B program is not just fraud: Trump official says it's a criminal enterprise; Americans will be very angry when the investigation is over]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133034009.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/h-1b-program-is-not-just-fraud-trump-official-says-its-a-criminal-enterprise-americans-will-be-very-angry-when-the-investigation-is-over/articleshow/133034009.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/h-1b-program-is-not-just-fraud-trump-official-says-its-a-criminal-enterprise-americans-will-be-very-angry-when-the-investigation-is-over/articleshow/133034009.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T18:07:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133034244,imgsize-1015024.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MacKenzie Scott gave Native Forward $50 mn; organisation reveals how it will spend it]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133031242.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Native Forward Scholars Fund has revealed how it will use the entire $50 million unrestricted donation from philanthropist MacKenzie Scott. The organisation will spend $10 million over the next five years to expand scholarships for Native students, while placing the remaining $40 million into a permanent endowment to provide long-term support. The gift, the largest in the organisation's 57-year history, comes as demand for financial aid continues to rise, with scholars facing an average unmet need of $26,000. Native Forward says the funding will help both current students and future generations pursue higher education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/mackenzie-scott-gave-native-forward-50-million-it-will-spend-10-million-on-scholarships-and-place-40-million-in-a-permanent-endowment/articleshow/133031242.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/mackenzie-scott-gave-native-forward-50-million-it-will-spend-10-million-on-scholarships-and-place-40-million-in-a-permanent-endowment/articleshow/133031242.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:47:08+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133032444,imgsize-77446.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Jersey police officer disguised as a roadside tree catch 74 distracted drivers]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133033500.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A New Jersey police department used an officer in a ghillie suit resembling a tree. This unusual tactic aimed to raise awareness about distracted driving dangers. Later, plainclothes officers conducted an operation and cited seventy-four drivers. These citations were for using mobile phones while operating vehicles. The campaign sought to reduce preventable crashes caused by inattentive drivers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-police-officer-disguised-as-a-roadside-tree-helped-catch-74-distracted-drivers-in-just-six-hours/articleshow/133033500.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/new-jersey-police-officer-disguised-as-a-roadside-tree-helped-catch-74-distracted-drivers-in-just-six-hours/articleshow/133033500.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:44:46+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133033500,imgsize-1489062.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Archaeologists uncover ancient Roman structure near the Colosseum]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133033402.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable discovery, archaeologists have unearthed a second-century building adjacent to the iconic Colosseum in Rome. This newly found structure boasts intricate mosaics and elaborately painted ceilings, hinting at its significant role in ancient society. While it bears resemblance to known firefighters' barracks from that era, some experts speculate it could also have been a luxurious Roman residence. Ongoing research aims to unveil its true historical purpose.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-uncover-ancient-roman-structure-near-the-colosseum-with-mosaics-resembling-firefighters-barracks/articleshow/133033402.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/archaeologists-uncover-ancient-roman-structure-near-the-colosseum-with-mosaics-resembling-firefighters-barracks/articleshow/133033402.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:33:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133033527,imgsize-279560.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Divers find 162-year-old Guinness bottle off UK coast, scientists hope to recreate historic beer]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133032819.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/divers-find-162-year-old-guinness-bottle-off-uk-coast-scientists-hope-to-recreate-historic-beer/articleshow/133032819.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/divers-find-162-year-old-guinness-bottle-off-uk-coast-scientists-hope-to-recreate-historic-beer/articleshow/133032819.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:26:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133033129,imgsize-933286.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Zealand’s rare woollyhead rises again with 250 new seedlings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133033278.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/new-zealands-rare-woollyhead-nearly-disappeared-from-the-wild-two-surviving-plants-helped-produce-250-seedlings-now-heading-back-to-the-reserve/articleshow/133033278.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/new-zealands-rare-woollyhead-nearly-disappeared-from-the-wild-two-surviving-plants-helped-produce-250-seedlings-now-heading-back-to-the-reserve/articleshow/133033278.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:32:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133033432,imgsize-188916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida’s nuclear plant became an unlikely home for American crocodiles]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133032268.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-nuclear-power-plant-was-surrounded-by-270-kilometres-of-canals-decades-later-american-crocodiles-turned-them-into-a-home/articleshow/133032268.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-nuclear-power-plant-was-surrounded-by-270-kilometres-of-canals-decades-later-american-crocodiles-turned-them-into-a-home/articleshow/133032268.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:14:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133032535,imgsize-1552847.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Minnesota retiree saved his new rod and landed a 2.21-pound state-record bluegill on day one]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133031308.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On his inaugural fishing adventure, Dale Hoffman snagged a massive bluegill weighing in at 2.21 pounds, breaking Minnesota's state record. This impressive catch happened on Big Stone Lake, renowned for its oversized bluegills, thanks to ongoing habitat enhancements. Notably, Dale used a new spinning rod, a special retirement gift, emphasizing the story behind this extraordinary moment in fishing history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/minnesota-retiree-dale-hoffman-took-his-new-rod-on-its-first-trip-when-it-nearly-flew-from-the-boat-he-grabbed-it-and-landed-a-2-21-pound-state-record-bluegill/articleshow/133031308.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/minnesota-retiree-dale-hoffman-took-his-new-rod-on-its-first-trip-when-it-nearly-flew-from-the-boat-he-grabbed-it-and-landed-a-2-21-pound-state-record-bluegill/articleshow/133031308.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T16:55:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133031588,imgsize-153693.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Martha Hunt’s Tribeca condo listed at $3.75M, nine years after $3.45M buy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133030997.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/martha-hunt-paid-3-45-million-for-a-tribeca-condo-in-2017-nine-years-later-the-1700-square-foot-home-on-a-hidden-alley-is-listed-for-3-75-million/articleshow/133030997.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/martha-hunt-paid-3-45-million-for-a-tribeca-condo-in-2017-nine-years-later-the-1700-square-foot-home-on-a-hidden-alley-is-listed-for-3-75-million/articleshow/133030997.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T16:55:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133031208,imgsize-85010.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discover Titan's methane rainstorms are more intense than expected]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133031872.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[On the distant moon Titan, intense methane rainstorms transform the icy terrain, creating striking alluvial fans that showcase the areas most affected by these rare deluges. Scientists leverage data from the Cassini mission to create models of these phenomena, which happen less frequently than once every Titan year—a period nearly equivalent to 30 Earth years. Understanding Titan's unique weather patterns offers insights into extreme rainfall events here on our planet.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-titans-methane-rainstorms-are-far-more-intense-than-expected-reshaping-saturns-largest-moon/articleshow/133031872.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-titans-methane-rainstorms-are-far-more-intense-than-expected-reshaping-saturns-largest-moon/articleshow/133031872.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133031988,imgsize-151426.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Galileo Galilei: "Passion is the genesis of genius."]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" 